# A max and a min of a parameter and a constant as loop bounds print as
# max and min. On an RTX 4090 micro_trip_max at n = 1 runs 2 trips.
# min.u32 compares unsigned: at n = 2, n − 4 reads as 2^32 − 2 and the
# loop runs 8 trips, where a signed min would give −2; with n bound to 2
# the operand leaves its type and the trip count is refused.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/trip_max.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/trip_max.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/trip_max.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/trip_max.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/trip_max.unsigned.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=UNSIGNED "%s"
FREE-LABEL: kernel micro_trip_max
FREE: trips = max(param_1, 2)
FREE-LABEL: kernel micro_trip_min_unsigned
FREE: trips = min(param_1 - 4, 8)
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_trip_max
CHECK: trips = 2
CHECK: $L__BB0_1  confirmed
UNSIGNED-LABEL: kernel micro_trip_min_unsigned
UNSIGNED: trips = unknown: `min.u32` of a value its type does not hold
